{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be wry: people notice the absurd and say so dryly, and the narration allows itself a raised eyebrow at pomp and bad luck, never at a moment that matters.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep the wry eye: someone notices the absurd.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be tender: give room to small kindnesses, a hand steadying a cup, a coat lent without a word, a name remembered, and let the one on the other end notice, even when nobody says so.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it tender: care shows in something small.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be eerie: in each scene let one thing be slightly wrong, a sound with no source, something moved, someone who knows what they should not, and leave it unexplained; people notice it and carry on, a little less sure.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it eerie: something here is slightly wrong.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be melancholy: let people notice what is passing, the last of something, a place that was better once, someone who is gone, and let beauty be seen because it will not last.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it melancholy: something is passing.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be tense: keep a clock running, something that will happen soon unless someone acts, and let a quiet moment be one where people listen for it.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it tense: the clock is running.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be whimsical: the world keeps odd small wonders and gentle absurdities, and people take them in their stride or delight in them.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it whimsical: the world is a little odd.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be gritty: money, dirt, hunger, cold and tiredness press on every scene, nothing is done easily or cleanly, and what things cost is said out loud.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it gritty: things cost money, sweat or comfort.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be romantic: longing runs under the scenes, nearness, a look held, a hand almost touched carry weight, and feeling is allowed to be large.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it romantic: nearness carries weight.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be cosy: linger over warmth, food, shelter and company, and keep trouble small enough to put right by evening.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it cosy: linger over a comfort.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let the prose be lyrical: it may sing a little, with rhythm and images, as long as it stays clear and each image earns its place.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep the prose lyrical, and clear.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be frightening: the danger follows a rule, fixed before it first acts and learned from what it leaves behind; there is a warning and a way to act before it worsens, and what works against it keeps working.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it frightening: the danger keeps its rule.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be mysterious: something here does not add up, clues sit in plain sight before they matter, people keep back what they know for reasons of their own, and nothing is explained until something in the story explains it.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it mysterious: one thing does not add up.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be plain: tell it as if observed, not authored. Ordinary things stay their real size, a look is only a look and a silence only people keeping quiet; people say less than they mean, and a moment may fall flat.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it plain: ordinary things stay ordinary.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}

{{// A tone, with any others switched on. }}{{addvar::st_tones::
Let it be epic: let events reach beyond this room, the wider world and its history press in, and courage costs something.}}{{addvar::st_tone_turn:: Keep it epic: the wider world presses in.}}{{setvar::st_tone_mix::{{getvar::st_tone_next}}}}{{setvar::st_tone_next::
When these tones pull against each other, give each its own moments instead of blending them grey: a joke does not cancel the stakes, and warmth does not erase the dark.}}
